HEVC V4L2 encode on Linux, and a hybrid VA-API plus V4L2 build.

is_linux is in platform_has_optional_hevc_encode_support, so the
renderer asks the GPU for an HEVC encoder profile. The stateful
capture fourcc V4L2_PIX_FMT_HEVC is mapped beside the slice fourcc,
and InitControlsHEVC sets B-frames to 0 and Main or Main 10.

fourcc.h and fourcc.cc keep the VA fourcc methods when use_vaapi and
use_v4l2_codec are both on. The image-processor test helpers return
null in that configuration. The production USE_VAAPI / USE_V4L2 order
is unchanged, so decode stays on VA-API.

